      "id": 1,
      "text": "Hampden was incorporated on February 24, 1794, and named after the English patriot John Hampden.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hampden%2C_Maine",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before its 1794 incorporation, the town was called Wheelersborough after settler Benjamin Wheeler.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hampden%2C_Maine",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Kinsley House Museum, the historic home of the Hampden Historical Society, sits on Main Road South.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.hampdenhistoricalsociety.org/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Hampden Historical Society began in 1992 as the John Hampden Society to honor the 17th‑century parliamentarian.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.hampdenmaine.gov/history",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1987, the former Hamlin law office on Upper Corner was relocated to the Hampden Historical Society grounds.",
